# SurgeGuard Security Alert App - environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` to override. Nothing here is a secret: sign-in lives in
# the backend's HttpOnly session cookie, exactly as in the Command Center.

# The SurgeGuard backend. The dev server (and `npm run preview`) proxies /api and
# /ws to it, so the app and the API share one origin and the cookie just works.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001

# Port for the app. 5190 keeps clear of the Command Center (5180).
# VITE_PORT=5190

# Interface to listen on. 0.0.0.0 lets a phone on the same Wi-Fi open the app at
# http://<this-computer's-IP>:5190. Use 127.0.0.1 to keep it on this machine.
# VITE_HOST=0.0.0.0
